      "reader": {
        "explanation": "For a Clique instance with target ℓ, take one variable per position, with host vertices as values. For each pair of positions, list the ordered adjacent host pairs in a binary constraint table. These tables require distinct adjacent images and have a clique as the primal graph, so its treewidth is ℓ−1 for ℓ≥2. After answering targets ℓ below two or above the host order directly, the tables have size polynomial in the complete source encoding.",
